# The payload under /usr/share/lazysite is a SOURCE tree, not run in
# place: `lazysite provision|upgrade` copies it into site trees and
# install.pl re-applies 0755 to .pl/.sh there (mode_for). dh_fixperms
# stripping +x here is therefore harmless, and the CLI/unit invoke the
# payload tools via `perl ...` explicitly.
lazysite-common: script-not-executable [usr/share/lazysite/*]
# CodeMirror ships inside the starter content because provisioned sites
# are self-contained (a site tree cannot symlink into libjs-codemirror;
# self-containment is the SM139 design - a host payload upgrade must not
# break a site that has not opted in).
lazysite-common: embedded-javascript-library please use libjs-codemirror [usr/share/lazysite/starter/*]
